<author id="1149436">jcb</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;So it is now equivalent to &lt;c&gt;binmode FILEHANDLE, ':raw'&lt;/c&gt;?  Point accepted, although it was a no-op when I learned Perl in the 5.6 era and seems to remain so absent the special configuration that you mention.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of my scripts omitting &lt;c&gt;binmode&lt;/c&gt; on POSIX have blown up, but I do not have &lt;tt&gt;PERLIO&lt;/tt&gt; set nor do those scripts &lt;c&gt;use open&lt;/c&gt;.  (Nor will those scripts ever be distributed in their current forms, as I know that they are not portable.)&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
